      {
        "id": "iE2EMANIFEST00000000000001",
        "title": "opv · e2e-app",
        "version": 1,
        "vault": {
          "id": "vE2EMANIFEST00000000000001",
          "name": "e2e-manifest"
        },
        "category": "SECURE_NOTE",
        "tags": [
          "opv-manifest",
          "opv-repo:example.test|e2e-org|e2e-app"
        ],
        "sections": [],
        "fields": [
          {
            "id": "notesPlain",
            "type": "STRING",
            "purpose": "NOTES",
            "label": "notesPlain",
            "value": "# opv managed configuration\n\nopv reads this note to know which keys the project **e2e-app** needs and where each environment keeps them. **No secret values are stored here.**\n\n- Values: in each environment's own item, whose ids are in the `opv-bindings` block below. Open one with `opv open KEY --env ENV`.\n- Change keys with `opv add KEY` or `opv config edit`. Hand edits are fine inside the first code block while it stays valid TOML; opv reads only the code blocks. The `opv-bindings` block is written by `opv apply`; leave it as it is.\n- About opv: https://github.com/matt-cochran/1password-vault\n\n```toml\n# The end-to-end test application (design §13.2). It holds IDs, names and rules only,\n# never a value: every field in tests/e2e/app/world.json carries a marker.\n#\n# File route:     opv --config tests/e2e/app/secrets.toml contract --json\n# Manifest route: OPV_PROJECT=e2e-app opv contract --json\n#                 (the item \"opv · e2e-app\" lives in world.json and its notes hold this\n#                  same TOML; tests/e2e/app/manifest/ keeps the committed copy)\n\n# Local development: no targets here, so the personal key is allowed. The team values\n# live in the two boundary items recorded below.\n[environments.dev]\ntitle = \"Local development\"\norder = 1\nboundaries.shared = {}\nboundaries.web    = {}\npersonal_vault = \"e2e-dev-private\"\npersonal_item  = \"e2e-app · dev (personal)\"\n\n# Production: locked behind confirm_env and one target per provider.\n[environments.prod]\ntitle = \"Production\"\norder = 2\nconfirm_env = true\nboundaries.shared = {}\nboundaries.web    = {}\n\n# The Fly target: one secret per rendered name.\n[environments.prod.targets.fly]\nfly.app = \"e2e-app-prod\"\nfly.secret_name = \"E2E__{PRODUCT}__{KEY}\"\nroles = [\"serve\"]\n\n# The Kubernetes target: the Deployment reads names from the e2e-prod namespace. Config\n# keys are ConfigMaps, and file keys are mounted under /run/secrets/<product> in the\n# e2e-app container only (the pod also runs a sidecar).\n[environments.prod.targets.k8s]\nkubernetes.context = \"e2e-cluster\"\nkubernetes.namespace = \"e2e-prod\"\nkubernetes.deployment = \"e2e-app\"\nkubernetes.container = \"e2e-app\"\nkubernetes.env_name = \"E2E__{PRODUCT}__{KEY}\"\nkubernetes.config = \"configmap\"\nkubernetes.secrets_dir = \"/run/secrets/{product}\"\nroles = [\"serve\"]\n\n# The GitHub target: repository secrets and variables, plus the production environment.\n[environments.prod.targets.gh]\ngithub.repo = \"e2e-org/e2e-app\"\ngithub.environment = \"production\"\ngithub.secret_name = \"E2E__{PRODUCT}__{KEY}\"\nroles = [\"serve\"]\n\n# A source-only home for a value more than one product reads. It is never delivered.\n[products.shared]\nsource_only = true\nboundary = \"shared\"\n\n[products.shared.keys.DATABASE_URL]\nkind = \"secret\"\nenvironments = [\"dev\", \"prod\"]\nguidance = \"the one connection string the fleet reads\"\n\n[products.shared.keys.FEATURE_FLAGS]\nkind = \"config\"\nenvironments = [\"dev\", \"prod\"]\nrules = { enum = [\"on\", \"off\"] }\n\n# The web product: its own keys, one shared key, two role-scoped keys, three file keys\n# and one personal key.\n[products.web]\nboundary = \"web\"\n\n[products.web.keys.DATABASE_URL]\nkind = \"secret\"\nfrom = \"shared/DATABASE_URL\"\nenvironments = [\"dev\", \"prod\"]\n\n[products.web.keys.API_KEY]\nkind = \"secret\"\nenvironments = [\"dev\", \"prod\"]\nguidance = \"the service's own API key\"\n\n[products.web.keys.LOG_LEVEL]\nkind = \"config\"\nenvironments = [\"dev\", \"prod\"]\nrules = { enum = [\"debug\", \"info\", \"warn\"] }\n\n# The serving process gets this; the migrating process does not.\n[products.web.keys.SESSION_SECRET]\nkind = \"secret\"\nenvironments = [\"dev\", \"prod\"]\nroles = [\"serve\"]\n\n# The migrating process gets this; the serving process does not.\n[products.web.keys.MIGRATION_TOKEN]\nkind = \"secret\"\nenvironments = [\"dev\", \"prod\"]\nroles = [\"migrate\"]\n\n# File keys: under `opv run`, their values are written into WEB_SECRETS_DIR at these\n# relative paths instead of the environment; on the Kubernetes target they are mounted\n# under kubernetes.secrets_dir.\n[products.web.keys.TLS_CERTIFICATE]\nkind = \"secret\"\nenvironments = [\"dev\", \"prod\"]\nfile = \"tls/certificate\"\n\n[products.web.keys.TLS_PRIVATE_KEY]\nkind = \"secret\"\nenvironments = [\"dev\", \"prod\"]\nfile = \"tls/private-key\"\n\n# A config file key: a ConfigMap item of the same volume on Kubernetes.\n[products.web.keys.OTEL_RESOURCE]\nkind = \"config\"\nenvironments = [\"prod\"]\nfile = \"otel/resource\"\n\n# Each developer keeps their own LLM key in their own item.\n[products.web.keys.PERSONAL_LLM_KEY]\nkind = \"secret\"\nenvironments = [\"dev\"]\npersonal = true\nguidance = \"your own key, billed to you\"\n\n[products.web.local]\nenvironment = \"declared_only\"\nsecrets_dir_env = \"WEB_SECRETS_DIR\"\n\n# The reviewed remote profile: a pinned host, roles and command.\n[products.web.remotes.builder]\nhost = \"builder.example.test\"\nuser = \"deploy\"\nhost_key = \"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIe2eMarkerHostKeyNotARealKey000000\"\nenvironments = [\"dev\"]\nroles = [\"serve\", \"migrate\"]\nopv = \"/usr/local/bin/opv\"\nworkdir = \"/srv/e2e-app\"\ncommand = [\"/usr/local/bin/opv\", \"run\", \"--env\", \"dev\", \"--product\", \"web\"]\n```\n\n```toml opv-bindings\nenvironments.dev.boundaries.shared.item_id = \"iE2ESHAREDDEV00000000000001\"\nenvironments.dev.boundaries.shared.vault_id = \"vE2ESHAREDDEV00000000000001\"\nenvironments.dev.boundaries.web.item_id = \"iE2EWEBDEV0000000000000001\"\nenvironments.dev.boundaries.web.vault_id = \"vE2EWEBDEV0000000000000001\"\nenvironments.prod.boundaries.shared.item_id = \"iE2ESHAREDPROD0000000000001\"\nenvironments.prod.boundaries.shared.vault_id = \"vE2ESHAREDPROD0000000000001\"\nenvironments.prod.boundaries.web.item_id = \"iE2EWEBPROD000000000000001\"\nenvironments.prod.boundaries.web.vault_id = \"vE2EWEBPROD000000000000001\"\nenvironments.prod.targets.fly.state_vault_id = \"vE2ESTATEFLY00000000000001\"\nenvironments.prod.targets.gh.state_vault_id = \"vE2ESTATEGH000000000000001\"\nenvironments.prod.targets.k8s.state_vault_id = \"vE2ESTATEK8S00000000000001\"\n```\n"
          },
          {
